{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas","id":1359363,"title":"Trinity Setting Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-06T15:36:03-08:00","id":1359363,"title":"Trinity Setting Ideas","content":"Obviously the Trinity Continuum is rife with setting possibilities. Besides the Core's &quot;Talent's in the Modern Age&quot; and the three classic flavors (\u00c6on, Aberrant, and Adventure), there's also forthcoming concepts such as Anima, \u00c6gis and IIRC Avalon. There's also been a number of interesting ideas bandied about in various forums (here, RPG.net, others).<br /> <br /> Just a few (my own and others):<br /> <br /> <b>\u00c6ther</b> - from MostlyJoe on rpg.net; basically Adventure but set in the 19th century and built from the tropes of period fiction. Genius detectives and their evil mastermind counterparts, amazing inventions, psychical research, clockwork men, monstrous misfits of science, and expeditions to the far corners of the globe and beyond (to the Moon, Mars, and the Hollow Earth, just to start).<br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius</b> - the great psychic awakening of 1969, with Psiads in the early 70s.<br /> <br /> <b>Action!</b> - the 80s action hero genre for the Core's Talents, in the decade that gave us Commando, The A-Team, Airwolf, Magnum PI, Big Trouble in Little China, Beverly Hills Cop, Lethal Weapon, Miami Vice, and Action Jackson.<br /> <br /> <b>Agents</b> - Again for Core Talents, the spy and espionage genre, both modern and historical (mainly the Cold War and James Bond type stuff)<br /> <br /> <b>Atomics!</b> - Like Adventure and Aether, but the world of 1950s sci fi, with giant mutant ants, experimental jets, alien invaders, and Godzilla.<br /> <br /> <b>Atlantis</b> - The ancient lost world.<br /> <br /> <b>Abiogenesis</b> - A weird idea for a modern or &quot;week after tomorrow&quot; type setting, with Superiors that are completely artificial constructions seeking a place and a purpose in a strange new world.<br /> <br /> <b>Abolition</b> - Another Core Talent one, about the Underground Railroad before and during the US Civil War.<br /> <br /> <b>Azoth</b> - from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>: Where Sir Issac Newton's interest in classical alchemy results in a massive flux event, and eventually voyages into the heavens that turn out to conform to Ptolemaic models. Sort of Gregory Keyes's Age of Unreason meets Richard Garfinkle's Celestial Matters.<br /> <br /> <b>Ares</b> - also from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> : Building of the Martian invasion of War of the Worlds to create an Edwardian version of \u00c6on, complete with Psi Orders.<br /> <br /> <b>Apex</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> again: Something of a sequel to Adventure, in which the heroes of the 20s stop the rise of Fascism and other totalitarianism statist movements, ultimately leading to a late 20th century Planetary Romance setting with Mars, Venus, and other worlds looking like they were imagined in John Carter and other period fiction.<br /> <br /> <b>Aftermath</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> : A post-apocalyptic Mad Max setting where China carried out the Ultimatum.<br /> <br /> <b>Allies</b>- Another historical one, with action-adventure in WW2.<br /> <br /> <b>Avast!</b> - from Medved on rpg.net, the age of pirates<br /> <br /> <b>Avant-Garde</b> - also Medved, with the Aberrant eruption happening in 1910, most of them aspiring to be Neitzsche's overman.<br /> <br /> <b>Argo/Argonauts</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> : Novas traveling the universe in their hyperadvanced space ship after the Ultimatum.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Armegeddon 1983</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1458\" data-vbnamecard=\"1458\">NewK</a> : WW3 in the 80s leads the Doyen to create the Psi Orders to preserve human civilization.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Aurum</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> : A sequel to Adventure, with Stalwarts, Superiors, and Novas in the late 30s and 40s.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bArgent</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> : Follow up to Aurum, with Novas in the late 50s and 60s.<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemy</b> (take 2) - Talents in the era and courts of Elizabeth I, Rudolph II, Christian IV, Michael the Brave, Henry IV, Sigismund III Vasa, Phillip II, and Pope Sixtus V.<br /> <br /> <b>Antediluvian</b> - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1601_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1601\" data-vbnamecard=\"1601\">Dreaminggod</a> : Prehistoric &quot;fantasy&quot;<br /> <br /> Aliens! - Something of an X-Files in the style of Hellboy/MIB/Stargate excursion into a world of government agents, secret invasions, and alien allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Anhk was suggested by CLAVDIVS as a \u00c6gyptian counterpart to \u00c6gis, along with Ado for Elizabethean/Shakespearean England. (Aesir or Asgard also work as a Norse counterpart to \u00c6gis.)<br /> <br /> <br /> And some random words that start with A that might inspire other people: Absinthe, Abyss, Academe, Acceleration, Achromatic, Adamantine, Ad Infinitum, Adonis, Aeolus, Aesop, Alabaster, Albion, Alexandria, Alloy, Aloha, Alpha Centauri, Amalgam, Amazon, Ambrosia, Amen Ra, Amnesia, Anagram, Analog, Anarchy, Android, Andromeda, Angelus, Animism, Antaeus, Antimatter, Anubis, Apparition, Apollo, Arabia, Arachne, Arcadia, Archimedes, Arena, Arsenal, Art Deco, Artemis, Assassins, Asylum, Atlas, Attitude, and Augustus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-13-2020, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T15:50:07-08:00","id":1359365,"title":"","content":"I actually named the one you have listed as Alchemy,\u201d Azoth\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T15:55:32-08:00","id":1359366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359365#post1359365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually named the one you have listed as Alchemy,\u201d Azoth\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you are correct. My tired brain keeps trying to insist on Alchemy.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T16:22:15-08:00","id":1359374,"title":"","content":"3 variations of Aether: One where all the Jules Verne stories are true. Another where all the classical monsters are real. And the last where Spiritualists basically scientific fact.<br /> <br /> Argo would be a nice name for a bunch of low powered novas that left Earth after the Ultimatum in a giant ship using the most amazing Nova Tech in the world, even Warpdrives and matter synthesisers, as none of them where capable is space flight. The name of the ship would be... Prometheus... OF COURSE IT WOULD BE ARGO!<br /> <br /> Amalgam would be a nice name for a Wuxia setting in modern world, with gangs fighting in the underworld for the pieces is an old Artifact that would become part of the user and he would be something more than human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T16:58:15-08:00","id":1359380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359374#post1359374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 variations of Aether: One where all the Jules Verne stories are true. Another where all the classical monsters are real. And the last where Spiritualists basically scientific fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking all three at once, with the Hollow Earth type stuff from Adventure, Mesmerist spirituasts dealing with flux ghosts, and Stalwarts including vampires, beastmen, and the like.<br /> <br /> And Argonauts as sane Novas or Superiors exploring the galaxy in search of a home, Battlestar Galactica style, would be pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T17:45:21-08:00","id":1359384,"title":"","content":"I have a few ideas. One is based on the Doomsday 1983 timeline where the third world war kicked off in 1983. In this one, the Doyen are good, or at least more neutral, and the creation of Psions and the rise of more psi-ads is a part of an attempt to save human civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T18:48:27-08:00","id":1359388,"title":"","content":"Aerthur-Talents of the Round Table!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T19:33:52-08:00","id":1359392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359388#post1359388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aerthur-Talents of the Round Table!</div> </div> </div> </div>Avalon. That game would definitely be called Avalon. Also if you look at the older stories, not just Talents. I\u2019m not saying Novas or Psions, but Stalwarts Knights of the Round Table should definitely be viable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T20:05:38-08:00","id":1359399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359388#post1359388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aerthur-Talents of the Round Table!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is what Avalon is alledged to be.<br /> <br /> I kind of want to try working out a setting based on Marvel Comics, almost entirely based on Talents, where various characters appear the year they debut and age in real time, and the technology developed by people like Hank Pym, Reed Richards, Tony Stark and others has transformed the world into a sci fi setting by the 21st century. (Mutants would all be Psiads probably.) So your factions would include stuff like the Future Foundation, Stark Industries, Xavier Academy, SHIELD, Heroes for Hire, the Secret Defenders, the New Warriors, Oracle Inc., and probably several others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T21:46:48-08:00","id":1359411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359392#post1359392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Avalon. That game would definitely be called Avalon. Also if you look at the older stories, not just Talents. I\u2019m not saying Novas or Psions, but Stalwarts Knights of the Round Table should definitely be viable</div> </div> </div> </div>And if \u00c6gis is anything to go by, Merlin would be some sort of psychomorph.<br /> <br /> Alternately, he's a high-tier Talent who, like Max Mercer, has a tenuous connection to time. (Or maybe he <i>is</i> Max Mercer?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-07-2020, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T21:54:22-08:00","id":1359412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359399#post1359399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is what Avalon is alledged to be.<br /> <br /> I kind of want to try working out a setting based on Marvel Comics, almost entirely based on Talents, where various characters appear the year they debut and age in real time, and the technology developed by people like Hank Pym, Reed Richards, Tony Stark and others has transformed the world into a sci fi setting by the 21st century. (Mutants would all be Psiads probably.) So your factions would include stuff like the Future Foundation, Stark Industries, Xavier Academy, SHIELD, Heroes for Hire, the Secret Defenders, the New Warriors, Oracle Inc., and probably several others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The X-Men are about as close as you'll ever get to people suffering from Quantum Flux. If I were to do this setting, I'd consider limiting mutants to low-powered Novas with mandatory Aberrations, much like the upcoming Deviant game for Chronicles of Darkness features people with Variations and linked Scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-10-2020, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T22:05:39-08:00","id":1359414,"title":"","content":"Aurum: an alternate sequel to the Adventure! era (late 30s to early 50s) but a bit more high-powered: not full-blown Novas, at least not at first; but where the eximorphs can be faster than a speeding bullet, more powerful than a locomotive, and able to leap real buildings in a single bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T02:49:30-08:00","id":1359434,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of an MCU-ish game with lots of Talents capable of creating Inspired Tech with Nova powers on it is nice. You can have a Hank Pym and a Tony Stark with no powers and no scale above regular people, but still capable of creating Nova Tech. They where even capable of creating Superiors by the 40s.<br /> <br /> the few novas could be Experiemntations, like Jessica Jones and Luke Cage, a few random dudes like Spider-Man, and some happy accidents, like the Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T04:38:39-08:00","id":1359450,"title":"","content":"In terms of Atomics! you could probably repurpose some of &quot;They Came From Beneath the Sea!&quot; because it uses Storypath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T04:47:31-08:00","id":1359453,"title":"","content":"I would actually keep Peter Parker as a Talent, based on the idea that the science demo results in a flux inspiration instead of radioactive spider, with him turning into this mix of genius inventor and investigative reporter in his teens, eventually graduating college and maybe joining the Future Foundation. Almost everyone would follow this trend, being a Pulp Adventure version of their secret identity rather than their super powered self. There may be a few Superiors, but the only possible Nova might be the Hulk. Mutants all being Psiads (and powers adapted to that) is partially to explain why they tended to get different treatment than every other super for so long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T06:35:16-08:00","id":1359470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359453#post1359453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually keep Peter Parker as a Talent, based on the idea that the science demo results in a flux inspiration instead of radioactive spider, with him turning into this mix of genius inventor and investigative reporter in his teens, eventually graduating college and maybe joining the Future Foundation. Almost everyone would follow this trend, being a Pulp Adventure version of their secret identity rather than their super powered self. There may be a few Superiors, but the only possible Nova might be the Hulk. Mutants all being Psiads (and powers adapted to that) is partially to explain why they tended to get different treatment than every other super for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously you could do this, but it kind of misses the core of him. Peter Parker is a very smart but fairly normal nerd (bullied by jocks, crushing on girls wayyyy out of his league). His first instinct on getting Spider-powers isn't to fight crime or save the world, but to get rich and famous because he's a poor nobody. The impetus toward him becoming Spider-Man is his guilt over failing to stop the criminal who would later kill Uncle Ben. <i>That</i> was his &quot;Inspiration.&quot; Otherwise Peter is the poster boy for the schlub who gets super-powers simply for being in the right/wrong place at the right/wrong time.<br /> <br /> Also, the stuff that Spider-Man does kind of requires levels of Mega-Strength (he can lift cars), Mega-Dexterity (he can dodge bullets mid-shot) and Mega-Cunning (Spider Sense). He probably also has at least a level of Mega-Intelligence to allow him to make his gadgets. One thing he would not have would be any kind of special resistance to lethal damage. Assuming you could shoot him in the head with a rifle, he'd die like any other normal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T07:20:21-08:00","id":1359482,"title":"","content":"Peter can be created with Superior powers, except for his clinging (and even that...). If you put on proper scale, all human super heroes in MCU are Superiors or low Q, except for Hulk (Q4) and Capitain Marvel (Q3)<br /> <br /> Even Quick Silver and Scarlet Witch are really underpowered (if you compare him to Quick Silver from X-Men movies you have the idea) and can be built as Superior (him) and Psiad (her).<br /> <br /> If you give Superiors and Talents the capacity of creating Novatech and Inspired Noetic items (not q tech nor powered Noetics), you can simulate most of the MCU with 2 Novas (Hulk and Capitain Marvel) and some powerful aliens (asgardians for exemple).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:00:24-08:00","id":1359648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359374#post1359374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amalgam would be a nice name for a Wuxia setting in modern world, with gangs fighting in the underworld for the pieces is an old Artifact that would become part of the user and he would be something more than human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to pick a good name for one that's full on Journey to the West, Investiture of the Gods Wuxia.... A chinese version of Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T22:55:39-08:00","id":1359655,"title":"","content":"The difficulty there is that, given the Chinese nature of Wuxia, I'd expect such a setting to have a Chinese name. And as far as I know, Chinese names never begin with the letter \u201cA\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T15:27:18-08:00","id":1359782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359655#post1359655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty there is that, given the Chinese nature of Wuxia, I'd expect such a setting to have a Chinese name. And as far as I know, Chinese names never begin with the letter \u201cA\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IT wouldn't nessiarily have to be a chinese name so much as a concept that translates into english.... of course we could also cheat and go with WuxiAe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T16:03:13-08:00","id":1359784,"title":"","content":"Well, by the Nexus rules, no book can start with A or \u00c6, so I guess we can just ignore this part...<br /> <br /> I am in a struggle with my Wuxia book title (I didn\u2019t even think about it until this morning...) any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T16:24:07-08:00","id":1359788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359784#post1359784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, by the Nexus rules, no book can start with A or \u00c6, so I guess we can just ignore this part...<br /> <br /> I am in a struggle with my Wuxia book title (I didn\u2019t even think about it until this morning...) any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a link to the Trinity content guidelines, I\u2019m having a hard time finding it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T16:49:05-08:00","id":1359799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/en-us/articles/360029073732-Storypath-Nexus-Community-Content-Program-Guidelines\" target=\"_blank\">https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/...ram-Guidelines</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T17:51:12-08:00","id":1359811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359784#post1359784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, by the Nexus rules, no book can start with A or \u00c6, so I guess we can just ignore this part...<br /> <br /> I am in a struggle with my Wuxia book title (I didn\u2019t even think about it until this morning...) any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Seven Strike as One&quot; &quot;Cobra Fang, Panther Claw.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, I'm just picking titles from episodes of <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3865236/?ref_=ttep_ep_tt\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Into the Badlands</i>.</a><br /> <br /> Figure you could do worse than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T18:03:39-08:00","id":1359816,"title":"","content":"Crouching Nova, Hidden Psion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T18:03:54-08:00","id":1359817,"title":"","content":"And crap, they\u2019re not allowing new era it looks like, I really hope they budge on that since it\u2019s kind of the point of the Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T18:10:58-08:00","id":1359818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359817#post1359817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And crap, they\u2019re not allowing new era it looks like, I really hope they budge on that since it\u2019s kind of the point of the Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost like saying you can't do new pantheons for Scion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T18:43:50-08:00","id":1359825,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that just means they don't want people creating products for Adventure and Abbersnt until they are officially released, since you know Kickstarter backers get advanced manuscripts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T18:52:19-08:00","id":1359828,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I'm thinking (hoping, actually) that the restriction on other eras will be lifted once TC:A! is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T20:45:57-08:00","id":1359837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359811#post1359811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Seven Strike as One&quot; &quot;Cobra Fang, Panther Claw.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, I'm just picking titles from episodes of <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3865236/?ref_=ttep_ep_tt\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Into the Badlands</i>.</a><br /> <br /> Figure you could do worse than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As much as I loved early Into the Badlands, I don't know how I didn't think of it as TC inspiration until now. Although I roll my dark eyes at a little bit of the last season, it is still a fun time.<br /> <br /> Really raises the question though, how would you model &quot;The Gift&quot; in TC? Superiors with a Condition, or two, on when they can use their powers? They aren't full on Novas, so like the Superior version of Dormancy almost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:09:09-08:00","id":1360037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359482#post1359482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Quick Silver and Scarlet Witch are really underpowered (if you compare him to Quick Silver from X-Men movies you have the idea) and can be built as Superior (him) and Psiad (her)</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Quicksilver in the X-Men movies is absurdly fast. He moves so fast that an explosion is going in slow motion and a bee's wings barely move. He's moving at several hundred kilometers per second. He'd have to be a nova.<br /> <br /> And if you mean MCU Quicksilver, he still at <i>least</i> moves fast enough that bullets are as slow as honey pouring from a jar. He's breaking the speed of sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 01-09-2020, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:15:31-08:00","id":1360042,"title":"","content":"Right. But Mateus Luz wasn't talking about the Quicksilver of the movies. He was talking about the Quicksilver of the comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:18:41-08:00","id":1360043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360042#post1360042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But Mateus Luz wasn't talking about the Quicksilver of the movies. He was talking about the Quicksilver of the comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quicksilver in the comics is wildly inconsistent, but even at his slowest he's depicted as moving at mach velocities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T20:52:51-08:00","id":1360045,"title":"","content":"One of the core ideas behind \u00c6ther was the flux barrier of the world is weakened. Allowing for reality hopping. <br /> <br /> <br /> Think Victorian Sliders.<br /> <br /> <br /> The catch being all the stuff bleeding INTO the World. See. Hallow Earth, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T21:54:49-08:00","id":1360053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360042#post1360042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But Mateus Luz wasn't talking about the Quicksilver of the movies. He was talking about the Quicksilver of the comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything that makes this even worse. With careful application of Thermokinesis, you can achieve a very limited &quot;weather control&quot; but you're nowhere near being able to do the stuff that Storm of the X-Men does, so she's clearly a Nova. Honestly, most of the folks in the MCU are either Talents or Novas. Scarlet Witch is probably a Psiad because Psychokinesis and Telepathy. Hell, Tony Stark is a Nova. Q-Tech is pretty much the only way to explain all the stuff the Iron Man armors can do. And if you go to the comics, he does way crazier things with them.<br /> <br /> Tell me how Thor is a Talent or a Psiad. If he's not a Nova then he's a Demigod/God level Scion, most likely. How about Thanos? Even if he's an alien, he'd still almost certainly have to be built as a Nova.<br /> <br /> Really I think a lot of setting stuff should be more about places that could exist in Aberrant/Aeon/Core but aren't likely to get a big, detailed write-up in an upcoming book. Figure any place with a Psi Order based there will get a big write-up. So will the Nippon Arcology. But... what''s going on in Russia. Or Liberia. Or Romania? Possible secret base of Aberrant on Pluto?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T22:22:46-08:00","id":1360061,"title":"","content":"As I read it, the setting in question was supposed to be inspired by Marvel comics, but wasn't supposed to be as potent as Marvel. That said, I refer you to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359412#post1359412\">my own initial reaction to it</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T23:16:18-08:00","id":1360072,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m honestly hoping we get an official 50s 60s Atomic! era. Maybe that\u2019s an off shoot of Adventure! where the Hammersmith energies increased over time instead of slowly dissipating, causing things to get even weirder.<br /> <br /> Aether and Avalon would both be similarly cool as official products.<br /> <br /> Heck, who am I kidding, I\u2019d love to have any of those listed in the first post as Eras, official or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 01-10-2020, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T23:21:47-08:00","id":1360074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359817#post1359817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And crap, they\u2019re not allowing new era it looks like, I really hope they budge on that since it\u2019s kind of the point of the Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I submitted a question about that to the Ask the Devs thread, so hopefully that will be clarified as to exactly what they mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T08:27:23-08:00","id":1360127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360072#post1360072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m honestly hoping we get an official 50s 60s Atomic! era. Maybe that\u2019s an off shoot of Adventure! where the Hammersmith energies increased over time instead of slowly dissipating, causing things to get even weirder.<br /> <br /> Aether and Avalon would both be similarly cool as official products.<br /> <br /> Heck, who am I kidding, I\u2019d love to have any of those listed in the first post as Eras, official or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could kind of get something like that with <i>They Came From Beneath the Sea!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:36:05-08:00","id":1360174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360053#post1360053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really I think a lot of setting stuff should be more about places that could exist in Aberrant/Aeon/Core but aren't likely to get a big, detailed write-up in an upcoming book. Figure any place with a Psi Order based there will get a big write-up. So will the Nippon Arcology. But... what''s going on in Russia. Or Liberia. Or Romania? Possible secret base of Aberrant on Pluto?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping some people will do some Nexus books similar to the short booklets that were done for the first editions (Psi Law, Media, Extrasolar Colonies for Trinity; the fighting league book and others for Aberrant). I could easily see updated versions of Media and PsiLaw, stuff about undersea colonies, Antarctica, specific nations, space stations, astroid mining, or the moons of the gas giants, as well as things like guides for doing Demolished Man/Babylon 5 PsiCorp style psychic detective stories, Psions as celebrities, and cosmic horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T12:08:59-08:00","id":1360182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360061#post1360061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I read it, the setting in question was supposed to be inspired by Marvel comics, but wasn't supposed to be as potent as Marvel. That said, I refer you to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359412#post1359412\">my own initial reaction to it</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. What I am envisioning with this is a 2020 where the technology is radically more advanced than ours, because people like Tony Stark, Reed Richards, and Hank Pym existed in the 1960s, not as super heroes but as inspired Talent geniuses whose inventions changed the world, and other inspired Talent adventurers also had significant social impact during the 60s, 70s, 80s, and 90s. (The turn of the Millennium would probably be my rough cut off point for Marvel characters, because you start getting too many to keep track of and I want the Players' characters to be the ones who are the movers and shakers of their present generation. But most of the organizations would clearly be tied to Marvel history.)<br /> <br /> This would be a setting primarily focused on Talents from the core book, with the following two and a half exceptions.<br /> <br /> The first is that all of the mutant characters are psychics and mostly exist in this shadowy sub-setting of their own. (I had originally considered them being Psiads from \u00c6xpansion, but instead am likely to go with each having just a single Mode, and some of the ones I pick for certain characters may seem counterintuitive to people. Since Quicksilver got brought up, I'll mention he would be a teleporter.)<br /> <br /> The second is the concept of the Weapon Plus program, starting in WW2 and having a very hit and miss record of trying to create Superiors over the decades. (This would specifically include Captain America, Luke Cage, and possibly Wolverine, among others.)<br /> <br /> And finally, I'm still debating what to do with the Hulk. He may end up being the setting's only Aberrant. Or Bruce Banner may just be another Talent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T13:34:20-08:00","id":1360191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360182#post1360182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And finally, I'm still debating what to do with the Hulk. He may end up being the setting's only Aberrant. Or Bruce Banner may just be another Talent.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a really powerful Psiad focused on Biokinesis and Vitakinesis who used super-science to create Attribute-boosting biotech Artifacts that he then incorporated into his own body. They're Flawed because the boosting only occurs in times of rage (the bioware/powers only come out when Bruce is the Hulk).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T13:44:51-08:00","id":1360194,"title":"","content":"I kind of have this vague idea in my head of using \u00c6on's stuff about Aberrants to develop some sort of &quot;Hulk cult&quot; of gamma/quantum mutated monsters, but it is very preliminary at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T15:06:13-08:00","id":1360211,"title":"","content":"Something which sees one group being transported to another world, and finding themselves Inspired, in part or whole, upon doing so. The players can do many thing but as the first set to be given power first in ranger agents work best at first. <br /> <br /> The group could be Romans, for the interesting idea of Romans in a fantasy world. Or the group could be from the modern day and transported by boat or plane or some mists cropping up over a campground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T15:34:30-08:00","id":1360215,"title":"","content":"I was working on the idea of Talents building Nova Tech (and possibly Superiors). Honestly Aberrant is great but after a few games it gets a bit overpowered, at least was the case in 1E, still didn\u2019t get to that point in 2e.<br /> <br /> This idea is very interesting and keep things under control... much like MCU, with \u201cnormal men\u201d using tech to fight gods.<br /> <br /> By the way, MCU Quicksilver is probably speed scale 4, completely possible for Superiors (Speedster 3 Power + Swift Edge + optional Free Running Edge), enough to be really close to Mach 1.<br /> Quicksilver in X-Men (future past and apokalipse) is faster... by far.<br /> But the comic Quicksilver can be so fast he can time travel and help himself, so... even the time stop thing is a bit newby...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:15:47-08:00","id":1360264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360194#post1360194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of have this vague idea in my head of using \u00c6on's stuff about Aberrants to develop some sort of &quot;Hulk cult&quot; of gamma/quantum mutated monsters, but it is very preliminary at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Knights of the Banner! They were a 2099 Hulk Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T12:13:56-08:00","id":1360362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1359414#post1359414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aurum: an alternate sequel to the Adventure! era (late 30s to early 50s) but a bit more high-powered: not full-blown Novas, at least not at first; but where the eximorphs can be faster than a speeding bullet, more powerful than a locomotive, and able to leap real buildings in a single bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which implies a sequel setting of Argent in the 60s as the Novas go more cosmic and absurdist on the power scale.<br /> <br /> This could actually be the timeline where Michael succeeded in the fight he and Max had in the 40s and he sets off N-Day early (in my head it\u2019s via the Trinity test, because that\u2019s too elegant and on the nose not to use).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T12:33:06-08:00","id":1360364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360362#post1360362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which implies a sequel setting of Argent in the 60s as the Novas go more cosmic and absurdist on the power scale.<br /> <br /> This could actually be the timeline where Michael succeeded in the fight he and Max had in the 40s and he sets off N-Day early (in my head it\u2019s via the Trinity test, because that\u2019s too elegant and on the nose not to use).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Aurum drawing some inspiration from the old Godlike RPG, as well as some of the superhuman (as opposed to Golden Age superheros) ideas in GURPS Weird War 2. Argent, meanwhile, could take certain ideas from The American Way and New Frontier, in addition to 50s and 60s sci fi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T13:39:04-08:00","id":1360376,"title":"","content":"The thing about the 50s and 60s sci fi that I would force into Aurum/Argentum would be all aliens are humanoid, no matter what. Of course there are alien dogs and cats, but they are not the important aliens in the planets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T14:55:24-08:00","id":1360384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360376#post1360376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the 50s and 60s sci fi that I would force into Aurum/Argentum would be all aliens are humanoid, no matter what. Of course there are alien dogs and cats, but they are not the important aliens in the planets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of some of the more off the wall stuff, like The Day of the Triffids, 2001: A Space Odyssey, some of Philip K Dick's stuff (Martian Time Slip, Now Wait for Last Year, The Unteleported Man, The Ganymede Takeover, Ubik), Heinlein's Stranger in a Strange Land, and kaiju films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T16:49:06-08:00","id":1360397,"title":"","content":"The same way that \u00c6gis is essentially looking to be \u201cScion, but Science!-based\u201d, I could see Argent being \u201cThey Came From Beneath the Sea, but with superheroes\u201d. (Well, Scion is also modern-day while \u00c6gis is ancient Greece; but then again, They Came From Beneath the Sea's monsters are all aquatic in nature, and Argent's monsters would likely be a bit more diverse than that. So the comparison may still be apt.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T00:05:46-08:00","id":1361224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1360264#post1360264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The Knights of the Banner! They were a 2099 Hulk Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Heroes Reborn had the Knights of the Atomic round table with all the genius going to University together and being in the group, including Victor Von Doom, and Tony\u2019s doomed friend Rebel O\u2019Reilly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What no love for my two favorite babies?<br /> <br /> Aphelion: Age of spiritualism exploration of a spirit dimension \u201cAphelion\u201d, Talent demon and Witch Hunters and investigators, Psi users channeling powers through rituals as mediums and spiritualists. And Quantum powers endowed by mysterious beings from the Aphelion turning men into Lovecraftian horrors. Mix theosophist conspiracies, Lovecraftian Eldritch mysterious, and early witch hunters and exorcists!<br /> <br /> Apeiron: my pet setting name for multiversal Adventures. One setting being a Solar system existing in the void of a post multiversal doomsday. Each plantary body from a different iteration of of our solar system. So maybe Nazi colonized mars unearthing Barsoom ruins, a moon with a breathable Blue Area and a colony of Inhuman Novas and an Alien Watcher. Each asteroid in the Kuiper Belt is from another universe so some may seem mundane others could hold O\u2019Neil Cyclinders from a human history unknown to us, an earth on the opposite side of the Sun still in the Pangea phase, the Earth maybe unique in that it\u2019s tve only planet that is composed of a Patchwork of different universes segments, so each region is from an alternate history. <br /> <br /> The idea being you start out on a Spacestation that survived your universe being destroyed. And the multiverse collapsed because of multiple mad science experiments across the Multiverse syncing up in a big calamity. Maybe their are universes unaffected but right now their are no stars in the sky besides the Sun.<br /> <br /> Basically original Secret Wars and Hickmans Secret Wars and Time Runs Out for the Patchwork Battleworld idea and multiversal Doomsday.<br /> <br /> And another Apeiron idea let\u2019s call it \u201cApeiron: The Trinity Continuum\u201d with three linked universes, and secretly a fourth world. Basically the Hammersmith event seems to have created three branching timelines. Each one with a sole Survivor with miraculous powers, (Burano, Mercer, Doctor Primorus). But instead of Mercer being a time traveler he is a universal hopper. With him allowing for communication being set up between the three they set up the Aeon Society. Each sets up their Universe based on their specialty, so Bhurano works on bringing Noetics to humanity, Divis Mal sets up Quantum uplifting, and Mercer collects tech and is more hands off resulting in a boom of Talents.<br /> <br /> Divis Mal eventually has a falling out and abandons his Universe when he discovers how to breach the barrier and and leave the trinity of Universes, taking many Novas with him. They treat his abandoned Earth as the poor third world and dump the Quantum infused blokes in this world as quarantine. Bhurano advances evolution and medical science and without quantum noetics blossoms. And Mercer\u2019s world accumulates information and tech with Psiad specialists recruited for projects. Only the Aeon Society knows about the Multiverse, but the Doyen are noticing the spikes of Quantum/Flux/Psi and try to quarantine Earth if they stumble upon the other universes they become a Doyen Trinity and works against humanity. All while Divis Mal builds a World Breaker Empire in the Secret 4th universe where no one survived the Hammersmith event, he starts to conquer other Earths beyond the Trinity.<br /> <br /> <br /> And another Apeiron idea is basically the Exiles Comic a team composed of individuals from different timelines hopping between universes on missions to fix the Multiverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T15:34:28-08:00","id":1361357,"title":"","content":"Love these two ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359363-trinity-setting-ideas?p=1361224#post1361224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking Heroes Reborn had the Knights of the Atomic round table with all the genius going to University together and being in the group, including Victor Von Doom, and Tony\u2019s doomed friend Rebel O\u2019Reilly.<br /> <br /> And another Apeiron idea is basically the Exiles Comic a team composed of individuals from different timelines hopping between universes on missions to fix the Multiverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former reminds me of a synergy of Black Summer and No Hero. Geniuses interested in exploring the human condition, push boundaries and ultimately coming to a head with the authorities. I was a big fan of Heroes Reborn as well as the Ultimates. I don't think the second happens without the first. <br /> <br /> The Exiles idea is great too. Reminds me of Black Science. While having real in-universe repercussions is satisfying, there's something pretty fun about being trouble-shooters flitting around the soft spots in the multiverse. Really, really makes it possible to keep retooling adventures to give everyone a chance to shine especially if you're working with talents, psions and novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}